# AN ENCLOSURE (M20).
#
# The M20 gate: a part with a draft, a shell and a counterbored hole, built in
# one script. All three name FACES, and none of them names an index -- what is
# stored is a sentence ("the top face", "every face pointing +y") that is
# answered again against whatever the part currently is.

# The block it all starts from.
sketch Base
tool rect
click -40 -30
click 40 30
pad Case 50

# TAPER the four walls first, so the shell that follows is hollowed out of the
# tapered shape rather than the square one. Order is not cosmetic here: shell
# then draft would taper the walls AND the cavity's walls, which is a different
# part.
#
# The neutral face is the bottom: that is what the enclosure sits on, and it
# is also the direction it comes out of a mould.
draft Case 3 bottom facing:+y facing:-y facing:+x facing:-x

# HOLLOW it, leaving 3 mm of wall and an open top.
shell Case 3 top

# `measure` reports what has been BUILT, so it needs a solve first -- before
# one, the features exist and the geometry does not.
solve
echo --- the enclosure, before drilling ---
measure

# FOUR MOUNTING HOLES through the floor. The points are the drawing: each one
# can be dimensioned or constrained, and the bore follows wherever it goes.
sketch Mounts xy 50
tool point
click -28 -18
tool point
click 28 -18
tool point
click -28 18
tool point
click 28 18

# No depth given means all the way through -- which asks the solid how far it
# reaches rather than guessing a deep cylinder.
hole Case Mounts 5

solve

echo --- and after ---
measure

save build/enclosure.ep3d
